# =============================================================================
#  NHL-DLBCL: repository exclusions
#
#  The repository carries code, protocols and result tables.
#  Bulk data and images go to a separate archive and are referenced by DOI.
#  Source datasets are never redistributed. They are referenced, with
#  checksums, in the tracked PROVENANCE.md files.
#
#  Excluded working-tree items at the time of writing:
#    DLBCLMorph.zip               30.3 GB   source dataset archive
#    DLBCLMorph/                  14.0 GB   extracted source dataset
#    kaggle_upload_staging/       13.9 GB   staging copies for Kaggle uploads
#    data/raw/.../cell_shapes.csv  356 MB   released source table
#    kaggle/ *.parquet             157 MB   derived per-object tables
#    kaggle/ *.png                 225 MB   QC overlays
#    reports/ contact sheets       130 MB   QC contact sheets
#    models/he.tar                 432 MB   third-party pretrained weights
#  What remains is about 20 MB of code, protocols, figures and result tables.
# =============================================================================

# --- Source dataset: 44 GB, not ours to redistribute -------------------------
# DLBCL-Morph is CC BY-NC 4.0 (TCIA/figshare). Download instructions and MD5
# checksums are in data/raw/dlbcl_morph/PROVENANCE.md, which is tracked.
/DLBCLMorph.zip
/DLBCLMorph/
/kaggle_upload_staging/
/data/raw/*
!/data/raw/dlbcl_morph
/data/raw/dlbcl_morph/*
!/data/raw/dlbcl_morph/PROVENANCE.md
!/data/raw/gse181063
/data/raw/gse181063/*
!/data/raw/gse181063/PROVENANCE.md

# --- Route 1 source downloads: about 282 MB, re-downloadable -----------------
# GEO series and platform files, PMC full texts and the GSE31312 supplement.
# Each file is SHA-256 hashed in route1/manifests/source_registry.csv.
# GSE181063_RawData.txt.gz alone (134 MB) exceeds GitHub's file size limit.
/route1/data/raw/

# --- Route 1 row-level extracts with exact calendar dates ---------------------
# Per-case diagnosis, progression, follow-up and death dates are identifiers
# under common de-identification standards. These files are regenerated by
# route1/src/wp1_gse31312_{extract,reconcile}.py from the hashed source PDF.
/route1/manifests/gse31312_table1_clinical.csv
/route1/manifests/gse31312_table2_outcome.csv
/route1/manifests/gse31312_linkage.csv
/route1/manifests/gse31312_reconciled.csv
/route1/reports/gse31312_extraction_discrepancies.csv

# --- Third-party model weights ------------------------------------------------
# models/he.tar is the LyNSeC/HoLy-Net checkpoint (Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.8065174,
# CC BY 4.0, 452 MB). Its provenance and MD5 are tracked. The binary is not.
/models/*
!/models/PROVENANCE.md

# --- Large derived artifacts --------------------------------------------------
*.parquet
*.pt
*.pth
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.zip
*.bin

# --- QC imagery: about 355 MB of overlays and contact sheets ------------------
# Manuscript figures under reports/preprint/figures/ are kept.
/kaggle/**/*.png
/kaggle/**/*.jpg
/kaggle/**/*.jpeg
/kaggle/**/*.tif
/kaggle/**/*.tiff
/reports/phase_03_e007_ai_contact_sheets/

# --- LaTeX build artifacts ----------------------------------------------------
# main.pdf and main.bbl are kept on purpose. The PDF is the readable artifact,
# and preprint servers often require the .bbl next to the sources.
*.aux
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.log
*.out
*.blg
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
*.lof
*.lot

# --- Python -------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/

# --- Local tooling, scratch and working notes ---------------------------------
/.tmp/
/download.log

# --- Credentials: never commit ------------------------------------------------
# make_and_upload_patches.py reads kaggle.json from $KAGGLE_CONFIG_DIR or
# ~/.kaggle. These rules are an extra safeguard.
kaggle.json
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*

# --- OS noise -----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
